            <exercise workspace="6in">
            <title>Partial Derivatives</title>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Recall for <m>f(x)</m>,
                        <md>
                            \frac{df}{dx} = f'(x) = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{f(x+h)- f(x)}{h}
                        </md>.
                       One natural way to extend this to <m>f(x,y)</m> is to repeat this definition twice (once for each variable):
                       <ol>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial f}{\partial x} = f_x = </m>
                            </p>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>\displaystyle \frac{\partial f}{\partial y} = f_y = </m>
                            </p>
                        </li>
                       </ol>
                         
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </exercise>
</page>
